1536
00:56:25,833 --> 00:56:27,067
Understand?

1537
00:56:27,067 --> 00:56:28,067
- [Joel] Okay, anybody
can open the door

1538
00:56:28,067 --> 00:56:29,400
when you tell me.

1539
00:56:29,433 --> 00:56:31,467
Wait, wait, I
wasn't awake enough!

1540
00:56:31,500 --> 00:56:35,233
What did you say?
(suspenseful music)

1541
00:56:35,267 --> 00:56:36,367
Shrew, puppy?

1542
00:56:37,200 --> 00:56:38,867
I mean shrew!

1543
00:56:38,900 --> 00:56:40,367
- [Crow] Aw, this
is just like Aliens,

1544
00:56:40,400 --> 00:56:42,367
except without the underwear.

1545
00:56:42,400 --> 00:56:44,667
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I
like the underwear.

1546
00:56:44,700 --> 00:56:48,067
(suspenseful music)

1547
00:56:48,100 --> 00:56:49,300
- Okay, open it just a crack.

1548
00:56:49,333 --> 00:56:51,167
- [Crow] Okay.

1549
00:56:51,200 --> 00:56:52,500
- Open it.

1550
00:56:52,533 --> 00:56:53,333
- [Joel] How come
I have to open it?

1551
00:56:53,367 --> 00:56:54,400
- Hold on to it.

1552
00:56:54,433 --> 00:56:56,967
(speaking foreign language)

1553
00:56:57,067 --> 00:56:57,733
- Okay.

1554
00:56:58,667 --> 00:57:00,400
- [Tom Servo] Freeze!

1555
00:57:03,833 --> 00:57:07,167
(speaking foreign language)

1556
00:57:07,200 --> 00:57:08,233
- [Joel] Well, this is
just like that Happy Days

1557
00:57:08,267 --> 00:57:10,533
or Perfect Strangers or
Full House or Empty Nest

1558
00:57:10,567 --> 00:57:12,067
or Just the Ten of Us episode

1559
00:57:12,067 --> 00:57:14,367
when they get stuck
in the basement.

1560
00:57:14,400 --> 00:57:15,800
- [Crow] Gin, vermouth?

1561
00:57:15,833 --> 00:57:17,800
This is where they keep it all!

1562
00:57:17,833 --> 00:57:20,367
- [Tom Servo] Ooh,
we can burn all this.

1563
00:57:20,400 --> 00:57:21,800
Oh, no, there's a
Teddy Roosevelt costume

1564
00:57:21,833 --> 00:57:24,567
and some graves down here!
(Crow gasping)

1565
00:57:24,600 --> 00:57:25,967
(suspenseful music)

1566
00:57:26,067 --> 00:57:27,167
- [Joel] Ahh, there's a
Muppet behind the stairs!

1567
00:57:27,200 --> 00:57:29,400
(suspenseful music)

1568
00:57:29,433 --> 00:57:30,900
- [Crow] It's all
right under the stairs.

1569
00:57:30,933 --> 00:57:33,233
- [Tom Servo] It's all right!

1570
00:57:34,767 --> 00:57:37,133
- [Joel] Honey, I think
we got puppets down here.

1571
00:57:37,167 --> 00:57:38,400
- [Crow] Hand puppets?

1572
00:57:38,433 --> 00:57:41,067
- [Joel] They're
under the stairs,

1573
00:57:41,067 --> 00:57:44,367
so I don't think
they're marionettes.

1574
00:57:44,400 --> 00:57:46,533
- [Tom Servo] Mr. Milkbones.

1575
00:57:46,567 --> 00:57:48,200
Rawhide chew toys.

1576
00:57:50,667 --> 00:57:51,967
- Mario?

1577
00:57:52,067 --> 00:57:53,167
- [Joel] Fine, thanks.

1578
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:54,067
- Aqui.

1579
00:57:54,067 --> 00:57:55,767
I see where he was.

1580
00:57:57,267 --> 00:57:59,167
I do not see where he is.

1581
00:57:59,200 --> 00:58:00,300
- Cuidado.

1582
00:58:00,333 --> 00:58:01,233
- Si, senor.

1583
00:58:01,267 --> 00:58:03,067
I will be careful.

1584
00:58:03,067 --> 00:58:04,367
- [Joel] Car full?

1585
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:07,467
- [Tom Servo] Oh, no, I
got shrew doo on my shoe!

1586
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:08,400
(suspenseful music)

1587
00:58:08,433 --> 00:58:09,200
(growling)

1588
00:58:09,233 --> 00:58:10,200
- [Joel] Ooh!

1589
00:58:10,233 --> 00:58:11,500
- [Crow] Weasels
ripped my flesh!

1590
00:58:11,533 --> 00:58:14,533
- [Tom Servo] Bad
puppet, bad puppet!

1591
00:58:15,833 --> 00:58:17,300
- [Joel] Would've
got here sooner,

1592
00:58:17,333 --> 00:58:19,333
but it's a big basement.

1593
00:58:21,500 --> 00:58:23,900
- [Crow] Please don't ask
me to suck out the venom.

1594
00:58:23,933 --> 00:58:26,333
- [Tom Servo] I thought you
said your dog does Macbeth.

1595
00:58:26,367 --> 00:58:28,733
- [Crow] He's not my dog.

1596
00:58:28,767 --> 00:58:32,667
Well, it's the booze
brothers to the rescue.

1597
00:58:32,700 --> 00:58:34,900
- [Joel] Beware the dwarf!

1598
00:58:36,567 --> 00:58:40,067
(suspenseful music)

1599
00:58:40,067 --> 00:58:41,533
- [Tom Servo] What is it, boy?

1600
00:58:41,567 --> 00:58:42,467
(gunshot)

1601
00:58:42,500 --> 00:58:43,967
- [Crow] We will prevail!

1602
00:58:44,067 --> 00:58:46,400
Our state fair is
a great state fair!

1603
00:58:46,433 --> 00:58:47,533
Try the veal.

1604
00:58:49,067 --> 00:58:50,667
- You alright down there?

1605
00:58:50,700 --> 00:58:52,500
- Doctor, get down here quick!

1606
00:58:52,533 --> 00:58:54,233
- [Crow] I'm fine, but
Mario's not doing so hot.

1607
00:58:54,267 --> 00:58:56,067
- [Joel] Oh, bad idea.

1608
00:58:56,067 --> 00:58:59,067
(suspenseful music)

1609
00:59:00,500 --> 00:59:01,833
- [Tom Servo] Hey, get off him!

1610
00:59:01,867 --> 00:59:04,500
- [Crow] No, he's got an
injury, see? (chuckling)

1611
00:59:04,533 --> 00:59:05,933
- Mario!
- Mario!

1612
00:59:07,167 --> 00:59:10,767
- [Tom Servo] Where'd
you hide the Cuervo?

1613
00:59:11,933 --> 00:59:13,700
- [Joel] Oh, he's got
rat scratch fever.

1614
00:59:13,733 --> 00:59:15,100
- [Tom Servo] Ooh!

1615
00:59:16,233 --> 00:59:18,067
(dramatic music)

1616
00:59:18,067 --> 00:59:19,133
Oh, well, look at the time.

1617
00:59:19,167 --> 00:59:23,200
I've gotta get to this
thing, I've gotta go.

1618
00:59:23,233 --> 00:59:24,233
- He's dead.

1619
00:59:25,867 --> 00:59:26,867
- [Tom Servo] He's red?

1620
00:59:26,900 --> 00:59:27,867
- [Crow] He's fed?

1621
00:59:27,900 --> 00:59:29,633
- [Joel] He's bed?

1622
00:59:29,667 --> 00:59:31,167
Oh, thank goodness!

1623
00:59:33,200 --> 00:59:34,333
- [Thorne] I got this
on him right away!

1624
00:59:34,367 --> 00:59:35,733
He couldn't have bled to death.

1625
00:59:35,767 --> 00:59:37,233
- [Tom Servo] Face
it, it's your fault.

1626
00:59:37,267 --> 00:59:39,133
- [Joel] Yep.

1627
00:59:39,167 --> 00:59:41,667
- Might as well let go of it.

1628
00:59:41,700 --> 00:59:43,067
Won't do him any good now.

1629
00:59:43,100 --> 00:59:44,967
- [Crow] Aw, get a body
bag out of the closet.

1630
00:59:45,067 --> 00:59:45,967
Can I have my gun back?

1631
00:59:46,067 --> 00:59:47,567
- What could've killed him?

1632
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:49,067
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I don't
know, maybe that shrew?

1633
00:59:49,100 --> 00:59:52,100
- I'm not certain,
'til the autopsy.

1634
00:59:54,167 --> 00:59:55,967
- Hematoxic syndrome.

1635
00:59:56,067 --> 00:59:57,067
- [Tom Servo] Sounds
like a Ludlum book.

1636
00:59:57,067 --> 00:59:58,500
- I'm afraid so.

1637
00:59:58,533 --> 01:00:00,733
We'll know after pathology.

1638
01:00:00,767 --> 01:00:01,733
- [Crow] Scatology?

1639
01:00:01,767 --> 01:00:02,733
They study dung?

1640
01:00:02,767 --> 01:00:04,067
Ugh.

1641
01:00:04,100 --> 01:00:05,200
- That's not the same
animal you showed me.

1642
01:00:05,233 --> 01:00:07,033
That's a monster!

1643
01:00:07,067 --> 01:00:08,033
- [Joel] He grew up!

1644
01:00:08,067 --> 01:00:09,567
- They are mutants.

1645
01:00:10,767 --> 01:00:12,233
- [Crow] Ted mute-gents.

1646
01:00:12,267 --> 01:00:13,167
- In controlling
the size factor.

1647
01:00:13,200 --> 01:00:14,133
- [Joel] Ooh, that's a stretch.

1648
01:00:14,167 --> 01:00:15,400
- They seem to have crossed

1649
01:00:15,433 --> 01:00:17,000
some of the other
characteristics.

1650
01:00:17,033 --> 01:00:19,133
- Well, you certainly
did a good job of it.

1651
01:00:19,167 --> 01:00:20,167
- [Joel] Well, thank you.

1652
01:00:20,200 --> 01:00:22,367
- I've known that for
some time, Captain!

1653
01:00:22,400 --> 01:00:23,833
- [Crow] Ooh, I'm sorry.

1654
01:00:23,867 --> 01:00:25,867
I had that coming.

1655
01:00:25,900 --> 01:00:27,667
- [Joel] Now I'd like to say
a prayer, if nobody minds.

1656
01:00:27,700 --> 01:00:28,967
There, done.

1657
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,000
- Mort!
- Would you please give me

1658
01:00:30,033 --> 01:00:31,000
a hand with Mario?

1659
01:00:31,033 --> 01:00:33,200
Radford, bring up the animal.

1660
01:00:33,233 --> 01:00:36,167
(dramatic music)

1661
01:00:37,367 --> 01:00:40,333
- [Joel] Tonight,
all dogs go to hell.

1662
01:00:40,367 --> 01:00:43,367
- [Tom Servo] Look,
he's levitating!

1663
01:00:44,833 --> 01:00:48,167
- [Crow] Next week
on Killer Shrews!

1664
01:00:48,200 --> 01:00:49,733
- [Tom Servo] Oh, turns
out it needs more vermouth.

1665
01:00:49,767 --> 01:00:51,833
Taste it, see what you think.

1666
01:00:51,867 --> 01:00:54,700
- Extremely high poison
content in the shrew's saliva.

1667
01:00:54,733 --> 01:00:56,000
- [Crow] But it's
smooth over ice.

1668
01:00:56,033 --> 01:00:58,133
- Now compare it with this.

1669
01:00:58,167 --> 01:01:01,367
Careful count isn't necessary.

1670
01:01:01,400 --> 01:01:04,067
Any indication the same
poison in Mario's blood

1671
01:01:04,067 --> 01:01:05,067
will give you the answer.

1672
01:01:05,100 --> 01:01:06,933
- Yes, you're right.

1673
01:01:08,233 --> 01:01:10,167
- [Tom Servo] Oh, I get it,
Mario's gonna become a shrew!

1674
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:11,467
- Look, Ann.

1675
01:01:11,500 --> 01:01:12,367
- [Joel] You know,
you're really a drag

1676
01:01:12,400 --> 01:01:14,567
on these weekend getaways, dig?

1677
01:01:14,600 --> 01:01:16,633
- Brooding about it's
not gonna do any good.

1678
01:01:16,667 --> 01:01:18,067
- [Crow] But breeding will.

1679
01:01:18,067 --> 01:01:20,367
- Now why don't you try to
think of something else?

1680
01:01:20,400 --> 01:01:21,633
Tell me.

1681
01:01:21,667 --> 01:01:22,967
- [Joel] Do you collect
plates or anything?

1682
01:01:23,067 --> 01:01:24,400
- Are you a scientist?

1683
01:01:24,433 --> 01:01:25,900
- [Joel] No, I sweep
up, what do you think?

1684
01:01:25,933 --> 01:01:26,733
- Oh?

1685
01:01:28,067 --> 01:01:29,833
That's the study of
animal act, isn't it?

1686
01:01:29,867 --> 01:01:30,900
- [Tom Servo] Animal acts?

1687
01:01:30,933 --> 01:01:31,967
- What do you specialize?

1688
01:01:32,067 --> 01:01:32,967
What do you specialize in?

1689
01:01:33,067 --> 01:01:33,967
- [Crow] Oh, nothing special.

1690
01:01:34,067 --> 01:01:35,167
- Their diet.

1691
01:01:35,200 --> 01:01:37,800
I had a hand in this, too.

1692
01:01:37,833 --> 01:01:39,067
- [Joel] If I had a hammer?

1693
01:01:39,067 --> 01:01:43,067
(wind whooshing)
(creaking)

1694
01:01:44,267 --> 01:01:45,967
- [Crow] I like
you, you're nice.

1695
01:01:46,067 --> 01:01:48,967
You're pretty, but you're
just a summer thing.

1696
01:01:49,067 --> 01:01:50,633
- But this ends it.

1697
01:01:50,667 --> 01:01:52,900
If we ever get off this island,

1698
01:01:52,933 --> 01:01:55,900
I'll never have anything
to do with it again.

1699
01:01:55,933 --> 01:01:57,067
- What will you do?

1700
01:01:57,067 --> 01:01:58,233
- [Joel] I'm going to
eat a lot of bacon.

1701
01:01:58,267 --> 01:02:01,133
- Like normal women do.

1702
01:02:01,167 --> 01:02:02,500
- [Tom Servo] Storm
the beach at Normandy?

1703
01:02:02,533 --> 01:02:05,867
- Dull after the life
I've been living.

1704
01:02:07,067 --> 01:02:09,500
I'd rather dull and
alive than excited and--

1705
01:02:09,533 --> 01:02:11,833
- I'll take a dull,
alive woman every time.

1706
01:02:11,867 --> 01:02:13,133
- [Tom Servo] I
guess the other way

1707
01:02:13,167 --> 01:02:13,967
would be kind of
sick, wouldn't it?

1708
01:02:14,067 --> 01:02:16,433
(upbeat music)

1709
01:02:20,600 --> 01:02:24,167
- [Joel] Goll, is this
hallway ever long!

1710
01:02:25,267 --> 01:02:27,167
- [Crow] Just
strain and stir it.

1711
01:02:27,200 --> 01:02:28,200
- Say Thorne.

1712
01:02:28,233 --> 01:02:29,533
- [All] Thorne.

1713
01:02:30,667 --> 01:02:33,833
- The autopsy has proved
